WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:05.530
This emoji is a total shit show. Apple completely&nbsp;
butchered it and it's actually kind of a big deal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:09.970
Think I'm being dramatic? Think again. This&nbsp;
is the lotus flower. It is a sacred symbol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.450
in a lot of religions, including Hinduism and&nbsp;
Buddhism, and it has a deep history in a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.550
of Asian cultures. The lotus symbolizes purity, a&nbsp;
beautiful, unstained flower rising from the mud.&nbsp;

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:24.130
Here's Apple's emoji, which looks nothing like&nbsp;
a lotus, more like a water lily, which isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:29.830
even in the same genus as the sacred lotus.&nbsp;
Lotus flowers grow on a stem above the leaf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:34.150
not floating on the surface like a damn lily.&nbsp;
And I know Apple likes their cute notches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.590
but lotuses don't have leaf notches&nbsp;
like this. This is a different plant.&nbsp;

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:44.230
There is a water lily that is called Nymphaea&nbsp;
lotus, but it is not sacred in Asia, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:49.690
matters because searching “Buddhism,” “Hinduism”&nbsp;
or “India” on Apple's keyboard brings up the lotus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:54.190
emoji. Searching “water lily” doesn't. Google&nbsp;
and other emoji designers didn't make this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:58.930
mistake. So how on earth did this happen? And&nbsp;
who can connect me to Tim Cook to get it fixed?

